# Story workflow

- Work on exactly one story ID (e.g. `M1-BE-03`) per chat. If the request names none, ask which story it is.
- Before editing, reply with a short plan: files, operations (`openapi.yaml` operationIds), tables, events and the
  tests you will write. Wait for approval when the user asked for a plan first.
- Write the story's listed tests along with the code. Run `make check` and report the result. "Done" means green,
  with Postgres running and nothing skipped (`AOS_TEST_REQUIRE_PG=1` in `.env`).
- Don't start work from a later story or milestone. Note follow-ups in the reply instead.
- When the story is done, tick it in `docs/specs/milestones/PROGRESS.md` and suggest the commit message
  `<story id>: <title>`.
- When a reference DDL file moves into `backend/migrations/`, delete it from `docs/specs/backend/ddl/` and remove its
  entry from `TABLES` in `backend/tests/test_reference_ddl.py` in the same change.
